# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# Note: .git is deliberately NOT excluded. The Makefile stamps the binary via
# ARG_COMMIT = `git rev-list -1 HEAD`, which silently degrades to "unknown"
# without it, and the builder stage is never published (only the `app` stage
# is, and it copies just bin/app, api/swagger.yml, assets/, migrations/, web/).
#
# Everything excluded below is either a secret or already gitignored, so the
# build context stays comparable to a clean git checkout.

.devcontainer
.vscode
.pkg
.tools-versions
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.vercel
docker-compose.*
docker-helper.sh

# secrets: never let a developer's local dotenv into a build layer.
# Dockerfile:245 does `COPY . /app/`, so without this a local .env.local
# would be baked into the builder image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.local.sample

# host build artefacts — all gitignored, and all rebuilt inside the image
bin
tmp
dumps

# runtime read-write volume: keep the directory (the readiness probe checks it
# is writeable) but never copy a developer's local contents into the image
assets/mnt/*
!assets/mnt/.gitkeep
